# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b2), edited. wilma_wainwright's first conversation.

~ start
set wilma_wainwright_met
Narrator: Down by the cellar steps smells of boiled cabbage, damp wool, and iron oil. A brisk woman keeps one hand near her club and an ear cocked toward the floorboards.
wilma_wainwright [neutral]: Wipe your boots before you tread mud across Mr. Tolliver's floorboards. Looking is free, touching is fine, and making trouble answers to Ronald and me.
* Ask about her work and the children downstairs -> about_self
* Ask how the village keeps safe in the dark -> about_village
* Ask what happened to the children's families -> rumour
* [Insight DC 13] Watch her face when she speaks of the dark -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ menu
wilma_wainwright [neutral]: Speak plain if you need something, I have three youngsters below and soup on the stove.
* Ask about her work and the children downstairs -> about_self
* Ask how the village keeps safe in the dark -> about_village
* Ask what happened to the children's families -> rumour
* [Insight DC 13] Watch her face when she speaks of the dark -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ about_self
wilma_wainwright [smile]: Mr. Tolliver gives us the basement and an honest wage to mind the post. It keeps a dry roof over Victoria, Eddie, and little Zachariah, Green Queen bless them.
-> menu

~ about_village
wilma_wainwright [neutral]: We keep to the Old Ways, bar the shutters at the late bells, and mind the Founder's Round. Strangers who respect custom do well enough here.
-> menu

~ rumour
wilma_wainwright [sad]: Those three little ones lost their folks to what comes at night out on the moor. That is all I am saying with young ears under the boards.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Her knuckles whiten on her belt, and her eyes flick toward the six quarters of the valley beyond the walls.
wilma_wainwright [afraid]: There are six great hungers out in this valley, and they do not leave bones to bury. Keep your lanterns lit if you walk past the stones.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
wilma_wainwright [angry]: Do not go prying after grief that is none of your business. The children are fed and warm, and that is what counts.
-> menu
